ios-flame bridge patch 0101 (MIT, 745c434), ported to metal2vulkan f6a96b7d by NegroniMetal: upstream removed PaddedReadsPolicy and Holds::Padding (every padded texture became a shadow). holding() lets padded rows and slices alias under PADDING_ALIASES (true), and aliases() takes an image whose subresources hold the padding up to the last row's pitch (padded_alone, the old Holds::Padding check). Since upstream e35bf78b every texture over host pages (each IOSurface the frontend imports) is a shadow before holding() is asked, so this reaches padded textures over the runtime's own buffers only. The unit tests follow the switch.

